  "interpretation": "All six videos contain legal multi-identity competition (47,500 rows), 33,507 rows with at least one unknown legal candidate and 21,261 rows with no known legal candidate. On clean-history rows, 4,212 legal-positive rows also contain an unknown candidate and 36,755 contain another known identity; 2,967 clean rows have no legal positive. The frozen baseline is top-1 correct on 132,879 of 132,894 legal-positive rows. These are support boundaries, not evidence that an online NULL or set rule will improve tracking.",
  "next_hypothesis": "Specify one unknown-preserving NULL/set rule with an explicit abstention cost and a matched no-rule control only if the rule can be evaluated without treating unknown labels as negative supervision."
